#: src/Admin/Settings.php:178
msgid "View requests"
msgstr "Ver solicitudes"

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:187
msgid "General"
msgstr "General"

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:190
msgid "Withdrawal period (days)"
msgstr "Periodo de desistimiento (días)"

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:192
msgid ""
"Statutory minimum is 14 days from the day the customer receives the goods. "
"The order has no delivery date, so the plugin counts from the day the order "
"is marked completed (or created, if it never was); a shipping plugin can "
"supply the real date through the withdraw/delivery_date filter. The start "
"day is not counted, the period ends at midnight of its last day, and a last "
"day on a Saturday or Sunday moves to the Monday (Regulation 1182/71, Art. 3)."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:195
msgid "Extra days (grace)"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:197
msgid ""
"Days added after the statutory period ends, for example to cover shipping "
"time when orders are completed at dispatch rather than at delivery."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:202
msgid "Refuse the declaration"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:203
msgid "Accept it and flag it as late"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:205
msgid ""
"A withdrawal counts as in time if the customer sent it before the period "
"expired (Directive 2011/83/EU, Art. 11a(5)), and the period runs from "
"delivery (Art. 9(2)(b)). If your completion date can be earlier than "
"delivery, accept late declarations and judge each one against the real "
"delivery date. Links in My Account and in emails still disappear at the "
"deadline."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:211
msgid "Form page"
msgstr "página de formulario"

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:214
msgid "Withdrawal form page"
msgstr "Página del formulario de desistimiento"

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:220
msgid "Select a page"
msgstr "Selecciona una página"

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:226
msgid ""
"Create a page with the [withdraw_form] shortcode, then select it here so the "
"My Account button can link to it."
msgstr ""
"Crea una página con el código abreviado [withdraw_form], luego selecciónala "
"aquí para que el botón Mi cuenta pueda vincularla."

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:235
msgid "Eligibility"
msgstr "Elegibilidad"

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:236
msgid ""
"Customers can only submit a withdrawal for orders in one of these statuses. "
"If none are checked, Completed and Processing are used."
msgstr ""
"Los clientes solo pueden desistir de pedidos en uno de estos estados. Si no "
"se marca ninguno, se utilizan Completado y Procesando."

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:249
msgid "No status checked: Completed and Processing will be saved instead."
msgstr ""
"No se ha marcado ningún estado: en su lugar se guardará Completado y "
"Procesando."

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:254
msgid "Where the function appears"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:259
msgid "Show a withdrawal link in the site footer"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:261
msgid ""
"The order view only reaches a signed-in customer looking at that order. "
"Article 11a asks for the function to be easily accessible for the whole "
"withdrawal period, so a footer link, a menu item or the [withdraw_link] "
"shortcode on a legal page covers the shoppers the order view does not."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:264
msgid "Link text"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:265 src/Frontend/WithdrawLink.php:86
msgid "Withdraw from contract here"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:266
msgid ""
"Leave empty for the statutory wording. Article 11a(1) prescribes \"withdraw "
"from contract here\" or an unambiguous equivalent, so if you change it, keep "
"it unambiguous."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:272
msgid "Guest access"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:277
msgid "Email a one-time link instead of opening the form straight away"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:279
msgid ""
"Off by default: a customer opens the form with their order number and "
"billing email. Turn this on and the form emails a one-time link to the order "
"billing address instead, so knowing the order number is not enough. Signed-"
"in customers reaching the form from My Account are never asked for a link. "
"This makes the withdrawal function depend on your shop outgoing email "
"working."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:284
msgid "Accept declarations that match no order"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:286
msgid ""
"When the order number and email match no order (a typo, or a different "
"address), the customer can still send the declaration with a description of "
"the goods. It is logged as not matched, without an order, and only you are "
"emailed: the address is unverified, so the customer acknowledgement is not "
"sent. Match it to the order and reply yourself. A status you set on it is "
"emailed to the address the customer gave."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:289
msgid ""
"This site is not served over HTTPS. The one-time link travels in a page "
"address and in a form field, so anyone able to watch the connection can read "
"it."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:295
msgid "Digital content"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:300
msgid "Ask for Article 16(m) consent at checkout for downloadable products"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:302
msgid ""
"Adds one optional, unticked checkbox to the checkout when the cart contains "
"a downloadable product. It carries both halves of Article 16(m): the request "
"to start supply immediately and the acknowledgement of losing the right of "
"withdrawal. Once a file has actually been downloaded, that item stops being "
"withdrawable. Virtual products that are not downloadable are services and "
"are not covered."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:305
msgid ""
"The box is never required. A customer who declines keeps the right of "
"withdrawal and still gets the download, because WooCommerce grants download "
"access regardless. That is the law working as intended, not a fault: consent "
"that is a condition of purchase is not freely given, and would not hold up "
"as an exclusion."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:308
msgid ""
"Turning this back off restores the right of withdrawal on past orders too. "
"Granting a withdrawal you could have refused is always lawful; honouring "
"consent from a feature you have switched off would be the surprising outcome."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:314
msgid "Emails"
msgstr "Correos electrónicos"

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:317
msgid "Notification email"
msgstr "Correo electrónico de notificación"

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:319
msgid ""
"Where new-request notifications are sent. Leave empty to use the site admin "
"email. The customer always gets a confirmation at their own address."
msgstr ""
"Dónde se envían las notificaciones de nuevas solicitudes. Déjalo vacío para "
"usar el correo electrónico del administrador del sitio. El cliente siempre "
"recibe una confirmación en su propia dirección."

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:322
msgid ""
"Every message this plugin sends is a WooCommerce email: same template, same "
"logo, same footer as your order emails, and each one can be reworded or "
"switched off on its own."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:329
