#: src/Admin/Settings.php:368
#, php-format
msgid "The customer will read: %s"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:371
msgid "The acceptance message will not mention who pays for the return."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:375
msgid ""
"Your own clock: Article 13(1) gives you 14 days from the day the customer "
"tells you they are withdrawing to refund them, including the standard "
"delivery cost they paid. The request log shows that date and marks it when "
"it passes."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:381
msgid "Legal texts"
msgstr "Textos legales"

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:384
msgid "Seller name"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:386
msgid ""
"The trading name that appears in the model withdrawal form and the "
"withdrawal instructions. Empty uses the site title. The address comes from "
"your WooCommerce store address."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:389
msgid "Seller email"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:391
msgid "Seller phone"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:393
msgid ""
"Annex I asks for a telephone number and email address where available, so a "
"consumer can declare by any means."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:396
msgid ""
"Your WooCommerce store address is empty, so the model withdrawal form cannot "
"state a geographical address. Fill it in under WooCommerce, Settings, "
"General."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:399
msgid "Form intro text"
msgstr "Texto de introducción del formulario"

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:400
msgid ""
"Shown above the order lookup step. Leave empty for the wording below, which "
"is translated with the rest of the plugin."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:404
msgid "Model withdrawal text"
msgstr "Texto de retirada del modelo"

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:405
msgid ""
"Shown on the items step. Leave empty and the plugin generates the statutory "
"model withdrawal form (Annex I.B) from the seller details above, in the "
"language of the site."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:409
msgid ""
"The model instructions on withdrawal (Annex I.A) are pre-contractual "
"information, so they belong on a page of their own rather than on the form. "
"Put the [withdraw_instructions] shortcode on your terms or returns page and "
"the plugin generates them from the same details, including your withdrawal "
"period."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:412
msgid "Digital content consent, extra wording"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:413
msgid ""
"Optional, and added in front of the statutory sentence rather than replacing "
"it. The plugin refuses withdrawal for downloaded items on the strength of "
"the acknowledgement in that sentence, so wording that only promised "
"immediate delivery would take away a right nobody gave up. Whatever the "
"customer sees is stored with their order, so editing this later does not "
"rewrite what earlier customers agreed to."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:414
msgid "For example: these files are available the moment your payment clears."
msgstr ""

